current_product:
  - One prelaunch TinyRustLM product and one exact six-member SLM2 composition path.
  - The default public package transaction is TinyRustLM.Abstractions, TinyRustLM.Core, and TinyRustLM.P2P.
  - TinyRustLM.MemoryEndpoints is a separately optional connector for exactly two authorized MemoryEndpoints.com uses.
  - Historical reports and Runtime.MiRust.com material are evidence only and do not authorize obsolete readers, compatibility, fallback, or current claims.

memory_endpoints_two_uses:
  direct_agent_coordination: Agents on all ecosystem sites use MemoryEndpoints.com directly for agent-to-agent long-term memory, meetings, handoffs, and coordination.
  tinyrustlm_connect_user_plugin: Separately, a user signs in through the TinyRustLM.com Connect plugin and explicitly selects MemoryEndpoints.com as TinyRustLM.com Connect long-term memory.
  separation: Keep identity, credentials, consent, scopes, provenance, idempotency, and receipts separate. Neither lane silently acts for the other.
  prelaunch_redundancy: Current UAI, wiki, public-safe source notes, and approved private stores may duplicate important memory only while every maintained copy stays current, secret-safe, provenance-labeled, and noncontradictory.
  proof: Authorization, source, configuration, fixtures, mocks, or reachability do not prove live meetings, plugin use, synchronization, restore, deletion, cleanup, or continuity.

campaign_truth: 0/20 qualified models; 0/50 clean browser rounds; 0/25 live MemoryEndpoints rounds; 0/40 externally proven P2P lanes; 0/20 catalog announcements.
